    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like people use the \"privacy\" argument just to stall actual progress. like, if we can use tech to make cities safer and more efficient, isn't it kind of irresponsible to let vague fears about \"slippery slopes\" stop us? it seems like the pro-security side has much more concrete, real-world benefits compared to these theoretical worries.",
